<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · mountain</p><h1 class="enc-title">Middle Atlas</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Middle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlas-mountains">Atlas</a> is a mountain range in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a>, part of the Atlas system, running north-east from the High Atlas towards the Taza gap. Its forested heights and plateaus, home largely to Amazigh (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a>) tribes, overlook the plains of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fez">Fez</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meknes">Meknes</a>. In the seventeenth century it was the base of the Dila'iyya brotherhood, which dominated much of northern Morocco after the Saadi collapse.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/middle-atlas.jpg" alt="Middle Atlas" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Иерей Максим Массалитин · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Middle_Atlas.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
